# TEMPLATE ONLY. This file IS COMMITTED to git. Never put a real token here.
#
# Copy it to ".github.env" in this same directory, with no ".example" on the
# end, and put the token in THAT file. Only .github.env is gitignored
# (.gitignore line 4). Verify with:
#
#   git check-ignore -v .github.env
#
# Create the token at:
#   https://github.com/settings/personal-access-tokens/new
#
# It must be a FINE-GRAINED token, not a classic one, because only
# fine-grained tokens can be restricted to specific repositories. That
# restriction is what keeps this credential away from work repositories, and
# GitHub enforces it server-side rather than trusting the caller.
#
#   Token name            barrage-claude
#   Expiration            90 days
#   Resource owner        your personal account
#   Repository access     Only select repositories -> Barrage
#   Repository perms      Contents        Read and write
#                         Pull requests   Read and write
#                         Metadata        Read-only (added automatically)
#   Account permissions   none, leave every one of them at No access
#
# Anything outside the selected repositories will return 404, which is the
# intended behaviour and not a bug.

GITHUB_TOKEN=github_pat_REPLACE_ME_IN_DOT_GITHUB_ENV_NOT_HERE

# Comma-separated allow-list of personal GitHub owners. tools/gh-personal.ps1
# refuses to run if the repo's origin is owned by anyone not listed here, and
# refuses outright on any remote using the github.com-work SSH alias.
GITHUB_OWNERS=DhruvT29
